Privacy Policy
TotalRecalls is built on a simple principle:
Your conversations belong to you.

We do not collect, store, or transmit your AI chats, session tokens, or export data.

What TotalRecalls stores
Nothing.

TotalRecalls does not:

store your chats

store your session tokens

store your passwords

store your exports

store analytics

store telemetry

create a cloud account

send your data to our servers

Everything stays on your PC.

Local‑only design
TotalRecalls runs locally.
Sign‑in happens inside a small embedded browser window on your machine.
We never see your credentials.

Session tokens
Your AI provider session tokens remain on your device.
They are not transmitted to TotalRecalls servers.

Export data
Your exported conversations land in a folder you choose.
We do not have access to this folder.

Crash logs
TotalRecalls does not automatically send crash logs.
If you want help diagnosing an issue, you may send logs manually.

Third‑party services
TotalRecalls uses:

Lemon Squeezy for payments

Microsoft WebView2 for embedded sign‑in windows

Both operate independently of TotalRecalls.

